Input: {"question": "What position does Comte de Digoine currently or formerly hold?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 143, "text": "In the quaint town of Fontainebleau, nestled in the heart of France, a man of great distinction and honor held a position of utmost importance."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 144, "end": 314, "text": "Comte de Digoine, a French official of the 19th century, was the esteemed sub-prefect of Fontainebleau, a role that commanded respect and admiration from the townspeople."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 315, "end": 478, "text": "As we delve into the life of Comte de Digoine, we find ourselves in the midst of a bygone era, where the echoes of the French Revolution still lingered in the air."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 479, "end": 610, "text": "It was a time of great change and transformation, and Fontainebleau, with its rich history and cultural heritage, was no exception."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 611, "end": 750, "text": "The town, famous for its stunning château and picturesque surroundings, was a hub of activity, attracting visitors from all over the world."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 751, "end": 868, "text": "Comte de Digoine, a man of refined taste and breeding, was the perfect candidate to hold the position of sub-prefect."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 869, "end": 982, "text": "As a member of the nobility, he possessed a deep understanding of the intricacies of French politics and society."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 983, "end": 1186, "text": "His appointment to the role was a testament to his exceptional administrative skills, his ability to navigate the complex web of bureaucracy, and his unwavering commitment to the people of Fontainebleau."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1187, "end": 1371, "text": "One of the most significant pieces of evidence supporting Comte de Digoine's position as sub-prefect of Fontainebleau is a letter dated 1850, addressed to the Minister of the Interior."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1372, "end": 1567, "text": "In this letter, Comte de Digoine reports on the state of the town's infrastructure, highlighting the need for improvements to the road network and the construction of a new bridge over the Seine."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1568, "end": 1741, "text": "The letter, written in elegant prose, demonstrates Comte de Digoine's mastery of the French language and his ability to articulate complex issues with clarity and precision."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1742, "end": 1916, "text": "Further evidence can be found in the archives of the Fontainebleau town hall, where a series of documents detail Comte de Digoine's involvement in various municipal projects."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1917, "end": 2084, "text": "One such document, a report on the renovation of the town's market square, bears the signature of Comte de Digoine, attesting to his direct involvement in the project."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2085, "end": 2344, "text": "The report, dated 1852, outlines the sub-prefect's vision for the square, which included the installation of new fountains, the construction of a grand pavilion, and the creation of a vibrant public space that would become the heart of the town's social life."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 96, "text": "As the sun set over the bustling streets of Melbourne, a peculiar figure emerged from the crowd."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 97, "end": 231, "text": "Comte de Digoine, resplendent in his tailcoat and top hat, cut a dashing figure as he made his way to the Australian Parliament House."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 232, "end": 391, "text": "The year was 1885, and the Comte, a French aristocrat, had found himself in the unlikeliest of positions - a member of the Australian House of Representatives."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 392, "end": 505, "text": "It was a chilly autumn evening, and the gas lamps that lined the streets cast a warm, golden glow over the scene."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 506, "end": 641, "text": "The Comte, his bushy mustache twirled to perfection, nodded to the passersby as he strode purposefully towards the parliament building."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 642, "end": 801, "text": "His eyes, a piercing blue, twinkled with a hint of mischief, a trait that had served him well in his previous life as a diplomat in the French Foreign Service."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 802, "end": 968, "text": "As he entered the grand hall, the Comte was greeted by the familiar sight of his fellow representatives, busily engaged in heated debates and whispered conversations."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 969, "end": 1129, "text": "He exchanged a warm smile with the Speaker of the House, a gruff but fair-minded man named Sir Malcolm Fraser, before taking his seat on the government benches."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1130, "end": 1214, "text": "The Comte's presence in the Australian parliament was a curiosity, to say the least."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1215, "end": 1384, "text": "Few could have predicted that a French aristocrat, with a reputation for wit and cunning, would find himself representing the interests of the people of Melbourne North."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1385, "end": 1488, "text": "And yet, here he was, a testament to the power of circumstance and the Comte's own irrepressible charm."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1489, "end": 1637, "text": "As the evening wore on, the Comte listened intently to the debates, his eyes darting between the speakers as he weighed the merits of each argument."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1638, "end": 1752, "text": "His thoughts, however, were elsewhere, drifting back to the events that had brought him to this unlikely position."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1753, "end": 1874, "text": "The whispers of scandal, the hasty departure from Paris, the chance encounter with a charismatic Australian politician..."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1875, "end": 1965, "text": "it was a story for another time, one that the Comte would keep close to his chest for now."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1966, "end": 2103, "text": "For the moment, he was content to bask in the glow of his newfound status, to soak up the atmosphere of this strange and wonderful place."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2104, "end": 2241, "text": "As the clock struck nine, the Comte rose from his seat, his voice booming through the chamber as he addressed his fellow representatives."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "sub-prefect of Fontainebleau", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "member of the Australian House of Representatives", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Comte de Digoine", "scope": "19th century French official", "claim": "Comte de Digoine was the esteemed sub-prefect of Fontainebleau.", "answer": "sub-prefect of Fontainebleau", "quote": "Comte de Digoine, a French official of the 19th century, was the esteemed sub-prefect of Fontainebleau, a role that commanded respect and admiration from the townspeople. As we delve into the life of Comte de Digoine, we find ourselves in the midst of a bygone era, where the echoes of the French Revolution still lingered in the air. It was a time of great change and transformation, and Fontainebleau, with its rich history and cultural heritage, was no exception. The town, famous for its stunning château and picturesque surroundings, was a hub of activity, attracting visitors from all over the world. Comte de Digoine, a man of refined taste and breeding, was the perfect candidate to hold the position of sub-prefect. As a member of the nobility, he possessed a deep understanding of the intricacies of French politics and society. His appointment to the role was a testament to his exceptional administrative skills, his ability to navigate the complex web of bureaucracy, and his unwavering commitment to the people of Fontainebleau. One of the most significant pieces of evidence supporting Comte de Digoine's position as sub-prefect of Fontainebleau is a letter dated 1850, addressed to the Minister of the Interior.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Comte de Digoine", "scope": "Australian Parliament", "claim": "The Comte de Digoine was a member of the Australian House of Representatives in 1885.", "answer": "member of the Australian House of Representatives", "quote": "The year was 1885, and the Comte, a French aristocrat, had found himself in the unlikeliest of positions - a member of the Australian House of Representatives.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["sub-prefect of Fontainebleau", "member of the Australian House of Representatives"]}

